From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:21:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: size the address scratch buffer for full-form IPv6

MAX_ADDRESS_STRING was 4*8+1 = 33 characters, but an IPv6 literal in
full form runs to 45 characters plus the terminator.  host_to_address()
rejects any address that does not fit, so no_proxy CIDR entries
silently failed to match a host written in full form.

Use INET6_ADDRSTRLEN, which is the constant meant for this.
---
 libfetch/common.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfetch/common.c b/libfetch/common.c
index ed7e098..b2db699 100644
--- a/libfetch/common.c
+++ b/libfetch/common.c
@@ -1044,7 +1044,7 @@ fetch_netrc_auth(struct url *url)
 }
 
 #define MAX_ADDRESS_BYTES	sizeof(struct in6_addr)
-#define MAX_ADDRESS_STRING	(4*8+1)
+#define MAX_ADDRESS_STRING	INET6_ADDRSTRLEN
 #define MAX_CIDR_STRING		(MAX_ADDRESS_STRING+4)
 
 static size_t host_to_address(uint8_t *buf, size_t buf_len, const char *host, size_t len)
